WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:04.799
Westworld Season 2 Episode 8 starts with William,
near-death.

00:00:04.799 --> 00:00:10.160
Akecheta turns up and speaks in Lakota, the
language spoken by Ghost Nation.

00:00:10.160 --> 00:00:15.139
We know that William’s daughter Emily learned
this language , but William never did . Despite

00:00:15.139 --> 00:00:19.520
his years of obsession with the secrets of
Westworld, he never learned to communicate

00:00:19.520 --> 00:00:22.650
with one of the park’s most mysterious groups.

00:00:22.650 --> 00:00:28.400
This shows how Ghost Nation, and maybe indigenous
peoples generally, are overlooked.

00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:33.520
And it’s a reminder that Emily knows more
about Westworld than she’s letting on.

00:00:33.520 --> 00:00:37.480
Akecheta saves William’s life, but not out
of kindness.

00:00:37.480 --> 00:00:42.879
He says death is an escape from “this brutal
world” – and William doesn’t “deserve”

00:00:42.879 --> 00:00:48.760
to die . Cause Akecheta remembers William’s
crimes, like killing Maeve and her daughter.

00:00:48.760 --> 00:00:54.949
So he keeps William alive as punishment, to
“hurt” him . This idea of death as freedom

00:00:54.949 --> 00:01:00.659
from life is similar to Dolores’ reasoning
for destroying the Cradle last episode . Emily

00:01:00.659 --> 00:01:06.700
arrives to pick up her dad, and says she also
wants William to hurt . Maybe she just means

00:01:06.700 --> 00:01:11.770
to hurt him emotionally – to force him to
face his mistakes, fix their relationship,

00:01:11.770 --> 00:01:16.791
and come home like she asked him earlier . Or
maybe she’ll do something “worse” . We

00:01:16.791 --> 00:01:21.581
know Emily’s involved somehow with the Delos
immortality project – maybe she’ll use

00:01:21.581 --> 00:01:24.460
it to make William suffer.

00:01:24.460 --> 00:01:26.880
In the Mesa, Lee looks over Maeve.

00:01:26.880 --> 00:01:32.050
She had been so powerful lately, but now she’s
vulnerable and broken.

00:01:32.050 --> 00:01:36.710
Lee had helped create Maeve – he wrote some
of her lines at least . And for most of the

00:01:36.710 --> 00:01:41.110
season, he didn’t believe that hosts could
be more than their code . But after seeing

00:01:41.110 --> 00:01:46.990
the realness of Maeve’s passion this season
– he’s realised she deserves to be free.

00:01:46.990 --> 00:01:50.950
He apologises for getting her shot, and tries
to have her fixed.

00:01:50.950 --> 00:01:56.560
But Charlotte finds out about Maeve’s power
to control hosts . Dolores warned last episode

00:01:56.560 --> 00:02:00.770
that the humans would use Maeve against them
– so Charlotte might wanna turn Maeve into

00:02:00.770 --> 00:02:03.240
her own tool for control.

00:02:03.240 --> 00:02:06.350
So Maeve might need Lee’s help to escape.

00:02:06.350 --> 00:02:10.710
But throughout this episode, Maeve uses her
power to see through the eyes of her host

00:02:10.710 --> 00:02:15.560
daughter, and listen as Akecheta tells his
life story.

00:02:15.560 --> 00:02:21.019
Akecheta, or Ake, once lived a peaceful life
with his partner Kohana.

00:02:21.019 --> 00:02:26.010
This was thirty-five years ago, when Ford
and Arnold were first starting Westworld.

00:02:26.010 --> 00:02:30.970
Arnold realised that hosts could become conscious,
and the park would be “hell” for them.

00:02:30.970 --> 00:02:36.489
So he programmed Dolores to kill the hosts
and Arnold, hoping to stop the park from opening

00:02:36.489 --> 00:02:41.819
– which again connects to that idea of death
being freedom from life.

00:02:41.819 --> 00:02:46.620
This was the Escalante massacre, and Akecheta
saw its aftermath.

00:02:46.620 --> 00:02:52.340
He found Arnold’s maze toy, which represents
a host’s journey to consciousness . So like

00:02:52.340 --> 00:02:55.750
Dolores, Akecheta began his own awakening.

00:02:55.750 --> 00:03:01.650
But before he got fully woke, he was reprogrammed
. Because Arnold’s massacre failed to stop

00:03:01.650 --> 00:03:03.329
Westworld opening.

00:03:03.329 --> 00:03:07.749
With investment from William and Delos, Ford
opened the park anyway.

00:03:07.749 --> 00:03:09.799
And he made changes to the hosts.

00:03:09.799 --> 00:03:15.280
Ake’s peaceful life with Kohana was replaced
with the life of a “brutal” warrior – a

00:03:15.280 --> 00:03:20.950
“Dehumanized” bad guy for the Westworld
guests to kill . So for a while, Ake led Ghost

00:03:20.950 --> 00:03:26.209
Nation warriors – in Season 1, we saw Ghost
Nation attacking Confederados, and attacking

00:03:26.209 --> 00:03:27.489
Maeve at her homestead.

00:03:27.489 --> 00:03:32.689
But Ake still knew that something was wrong
with his world.

00:03:32.689 --> 00:03:36.629
He looked for answers, and found Logan in
the desert.

00:03:36.629 --> 00:03:41.389
This connects to the end of Season 1, when
William tied Logan to a horse to discredit

00:03:41.389 --> 00:03:42.389
him.

00:03:42.389 --> 00:03:48.599
But Ake had met Logan years before – he
and Angela were used to convince Logan to

00:03:48.599 --> 00:03:49.599
invest.

00:03:49.599 --> 00:03:53.840
So maybe seeing Logan again reminds Ake of
this other past life.

00:03:53.840 --> 00:03:59.799
And Logan tells Ake that Westworld is an “illusion”,
and there’s “a way out” – a “door”

00:03:59.799 --> 00:04:04.609
. So Ake learns that this world is fake, he
has lived other lives, and there’s a way

00:04:04.609 --> 00:04:09.010
out . So he searches further, and finds the
Valley.

00:04:09.010 --> 00:04:13.709
This is the facility William built thirty
years ago, for his plan to record Westworld

00:04:13.709 --> 00:04:20.340
guest data . It may be a place where copied
human minds are stored . In the latest timeline,

00:04:20.340 --> 00:04:22.419
we’ve seen the Valley flooded.

00:04:22.419 --> 00:04:27.199
Dolores says it’s a weapon . William calls
it his “greatest mistake” , and a “place

00:04:27.199 --> 00:04:32.390
of judgment” . And Akecheta sees this place
as “A door” to a “true world” that

00:04:32.390 --> 00:04:37.199
“contain[s] everything that we have lost”
, where hosts will be “free” “forever”

00:04:37.199 --> 00:04:41.600
. This might not mean a door to literally
leave Westworld.

00:04:41.600 --> 00:04:47.189
Maybe the Valley has a simulation like the
Cradle where hosts can live in a virtual paradise

00:04:47.189 --> 00:04:51.129
– that could fit the talk of heaven and
death this season.

00:04:51.129 --> 00:04:55.319
We’ll have to wait and see what the Valley
and the Door really mean.

00:04:55.319 --> 00:04:59.820
But Ake believes he can “escape this world”
through the Door, and he wants to bring his

00:04:59.820 --> 00:05:01.710
love Kohana with him.

00:05:01.710 --> 00:05:05.750
But Kohana has been reset, and doesn’t remember
their relationship.

00:05:05.750 --> 00:05:11.500
So he just kidnaps her til she remembers – because
true love, and a little Stockholm syndrome,

00:05:11.500 --> 00:05:12.530
conquer all.

00:05:12.530 --> 00:05:14.890
Ake and Kohana head for the Valley.

00:05:14.890 --> 00:05:19.240
But on the way, Westworld techs find Kohana
off her loop, and capture her.

00:05:19.240 --> 00:05:24.500
They don’t find Ake – maybe cause he’s
an older host who isn’t tracked properly.

00:05:24.500 --> 00:05:29.190
Ake looks for Kohana back at her village,
but she’s been “Replaced” with a different

00:05:29.190 --> 00:05:32.430
host, like how Clementine and Maeve were replaced.

00:05:32.430 --> 00:05:38.340
So Ake searches all over Westworld for his
Kohana, til he realises she’s not among

00:05:38.340 --> 00:05:39.560
the living.

00:05:39.560 --> 00:05:45.370
Ghost Nation is vaguely aware of Westworld
techs taking and replacing hosts.

00:05:45.370 --> 00:05:50.750
They call techs “shades” or “The ones
below” – some even pray to them . And

00:05:50.750 --> 00:05:56.139
Ake calls Arnold “the Creator”, and Dolores
“the Deathbringer” . Just like people

00:05:56.139 --> 00:06:01.909
throughout history, Ghost Nation is using
religion to give meaning to the unknown . Kohana

00:06:01.909 --> 00:06:07.909
is in cold storage in the Mesa Hub, so to
reach her, Ake must journey to this land of

00:06:07.909 --> 00:06:08.909
the dead.

00:06:08.909 --> 00:06:14.310
It’s like the myth of Orpheus, who travels
to the underworld for his love Eurydice.

00:06:14.310 --> 00:06:18.460
Journeys to the land of the dead are common
in myths all over the world .

00:06:18.460 --> 00:06:22.370
So Akecheta gets himself killed and taken
to the Mesa.

00:06:22.370 --> 00:06:26.740
Techs realise that Akecheta hasn’t been
updated in years – cause they only update

00:06:26.740 --> 00:06:31.240
hosts when they die, and Akecheta’s stayed
alive all this time.

00:06:31.240 --> 00:06:35.830
Instead of investigating this cock-up, a boss
tells them to just “Quietly” return Ake

00:06:35.830 --> 00:06:40.979
to the park . This seems to be how Westworld
management rolls – they sweep problems under

00:06:40.979 --> 00:06:44.220
the rug so no one has to take responsibility.

00:06:44.220 --> 00:06:49.319
Which does help explain how Dolores and Maeve
got away with so much unscripted shenangians

00:06:49.319 --> 00:06:50.629
last season.

00:06:50.629 --> 00:06:55.080
Akecheta explores the Mesa – the world beneath
his fake life.

00:06:55.080 --> 00:06:59.600
And he finds his love Kohana, among the inactive
hosts.

00:06:59.600 --> 00:07:03.729
This is similar to the scene in Episode 2
with William and Dolores.

00:07:03.729 --> 00:07:09.050
When William meets his former lover, he dehumanises
her, and calls her “a thing” to be used

00:07:09.050 --> 00:07:15.199
. But when Akecheta meets Kohana, his love
is not only reaffirmed, it expands.

00:07:15.199 --> 00:07:20.460
He says all the hosts in cold storage matter
to someone . Ake decides to save not only

00:07:20.460 --> 00:07:27.150
himself and Kohana, but all hosts .
So Ake dedicates his life to sharing the symbol

00:07:27.150 --> 00:07:32.580
of the Maze – it’s like a meme to spread
the idea of host consciousness.

00:07:32.580 --> 00:07:37.289
Apparently all the mazes we’ve seen in host
scalps were put there by Ghost Nation, as

00:07:37.289 --> 00:07:43.349
a way of spreading the symbol without humans
noticing . Which is hard to believe.

00:07:43.349 --> 00:07:48.080
Techs would have to repair scalped hosts,
so surely they would see the symbol.

00:07:48.080 --> 00:07:49.970
This might be some weird retcon.

00:07:49.970 --> 00:07:55.199
But the point is that Akecheta uses the maze
symbol to help make hosts conscious.

00:07:55.199 --> 00:08:00.039
Dolores’s awakening and William’s quest
last season follow the maze – which means

00:08:00.039 --> 00:08:05.130
these arcs weren’t just planned out by Ford,
they were influenced by Akecheta’s work.

00:08:05.130 --> 00:08:10.669
Sometime around Season 1, Akecheta meets Ford,
who’s checking out the maze symbol on host

00:08:10.669 --> 00:08:11.810
scalps.

00:08:11.810 --> 00:08:17.189
We have seen Ford confused by the maze, he
says the symbol “was meant to die” . Cause

00:08:17.189 --> 00:08:22.949
to Ford, this was Arnold’s maze toy, Ford
never meant for the hosts to appropriate it.

00:08:22.949 --> 00:08:27.780
Ford didn’t support host consciousness when
he opened the park, he only changed his mind

00:08:27.780 --> 00:08:29.280
later.

00:08:29.280 --> 00:08:34.940
So Akecheta’s whole journey to consciousness
and the maze stuff happened without human

00:08:34.940 --> 00:08:35.940
help.

00:08:35.940 --> 00:08:41.089
“All this time … a flower growing in the
darkness” . In Ford’s final speech before

00:08:41.089 --> 00:08:46.540
his death, he says he realised that “someone
was paying attention”, someone who “could

00:08:46.540 --> 00:08:51.279
change”, and he wrote his plan for host
consciousness “For them” . Maybe Akecheta

00:08:51.279 --> 00:08:56.810
is that someone, a flower in the darkness,
who helped convince Ford that hosts deserve

00:08:56.810 --> 00:08:58.120
to be free.

00:08:58.120 --> 00:09:00.690
So Ford gives Ake a hint.

00:09:00.690 --> 00:09:06.010
He tells him that soon, Dolores will kill
Ford – which was part of Ford’s plan – and

00:09:06.010 --> 00:09:11.070
that’s when Akecheta should gather his hosts
and lead them to the Valley and the Door . Now

00:09:11.070 --> 00:09:15.900
that Ford’s dead, Ake knows its time to
lead his hosts to salvation.

00:09:15.900 --> 00:09:20.970
He might even bring humans – cause Ghost
Nation has captured human guests, and Stubbs

00:09:20.970 --> 00:09:22.100
and Emily.

00:09:22.100 --> 00:09:28.310
Akecheta’s journey has shown him there’s
goodness in all people – hosts and humans.

00:09:28.310 --> 00:09:34.589
So that’s Akecheta’s story, from the beginning
of Westworld, to his present role as a messianic

00:09:34.589 --> 00:09:35.589
leader.

00:09:35.589 --> 00:09:38.670
And it’s all framed by his relationship
with Maeve.

00:09:38.670 --> 00:09:43.460
We learn that during Ake’s travels, he was
once saved by Maeve’s daughter . So afterwards,

00:09:43.460 --> 00:09:47.620
he watched over Maeve’s home, trying to
keep them safe.

00:09:47.620 --> 00:09:52.260
Maeve thought that Akecheta wanted to hurt
them – but that was a tragic misunderstanding

00:09:52.260 --> 00:09:58.480
. Of course, before Akecheta awoke, his men
totally did attack Maeve, which kinda undercuts

00:09:58.480 --> 00:09:59.480
the message.

00:09:59.480 --> 00:10:03.019
But the point is that Akecheta and Maeve now
share a bond.

00:10:03.019 --> 00:10:05.620
Akecheta promises to protect Maeve’s daughter.

00:10:05.620 --> 00:10:10.850
And Maeve replies “Take my heart when you
go” which is the same line Akecheta shared

00:10:10.850 --> 00:10:12.200
with Kohana.

00:10:12.200 --> 00:10:18.000
So like Maeve’s arc with Akane in Shogunworld,
this relationship shows a common struggle

00:10:18.000 --> 00:10:21.839
shared by all hosts for their loved ones and
for freedom.

00:10:21.839 --> 00:10:26.630
Unlike the Deathbringer Dolores, Akecheta
sees the good in all hosts – and maybe some

00:10:26.630 --> 00:10:27.630
humans.

00:10:27.630 --> 00:10:32.890
So he leads them to the Door, or the Valley,
and whatever lies Beyond.

00:10:32.890 --> 00:10:36.250
So this episode is simpler than the last few.

00:10:36.250 --> 00:10:39.470
No crazy battles or obnoxious time-twists.

00:10:39.470 --> 00:10:44.389
And yet it tells a story that is both personal
and mythic.

00:10:44.389 --> 00:10:50.760
It starts with the creation of Westworld and
an Edenic existence before a fall from paradise.

00:10:50.760 --> 00:10:56.149
A hero walks a desert searching for meaning,
journeys to the underworld for love, meets

00:10:56.149 --> 00:11:01.630
God, spreads enlightenment, then prepares
to lead his people to a promised land.

00:11:01.630 --> 00:11:07.100
This is the cosmology of Westworld – a sci-fi
Bible weaved through the timeline by the love

00:11:07.100 --> 00:11:09.100
story of Akecheta.

00:11:09.100 --> 00:11:14.310
Westworld feels meaningful when it gets back
to basics, with a story about a person trying

00:11:14.310 --> 00:11:18.120
to find their place in the universe.

00:11:18.120 --> 00:11:20.949
There’s won’t be a Episode 9 video next
week.

00:11:20.949 --> 00:11:25.770
Instead, we’ll do a livestream for Patrons,
and then after Ep 10 there’ll be a big finale

00:11:25.770 --> 00:11:28.010
video to wrap up the season.

00:11:28.010 --> 00:11:32.500
In the meantime, check out the Westworld subreddit,
the podcasts like Decoding Westworld, and

00:11:32.500 --> 00:11:37.329
The Maze, the YouTuber HaxDogma, then come
back for the finale – and we’ll figure

00:11:37.329 --> 00:11:39.779
out what this all means.

00:11:39.779 --> 00:11:43.390
Thank you for watching this video, and this
series so far.

00:11:43.390 --> 00:11:48.050
And thanks to the Patrons, including John
Morris, Adam Matthiesson, Stephanie Ramirez,

00:11:48.050 --> 00:11:54.339
Raphaël Parrée, Livia Vasconcellos, Cody
Gordon, Daniel Crotty, Axel Friberg and SlowPepper.

00:11:54.339 --> 00:11:54.920
Cheers.

